  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **ROLLIN BACK**: back after 40 archived shows (705 days) [3]\n- **LIBRARIAN**: back after 39 archived shows (644 days) [3]\n- **ROCKET MAN (ELTON JOHN)**: rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **TONIGHT I WANT TO CELEBRATE WITH YOU**: back after 40 archived shows (705 days) [3]\n- **TYRONE (ERYKAH BADU)**: back after 37 archived shows (430 days) [3]\n- **WHAT A WONDERFUL MAN**: back after 28 archived shows (401 days) [3]\n- **IT'S ABOUT TWILIGHT NOW**: back after 92 archived shows (2043 days) [3]\n- **NEVER TEAR US APART (INXS)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2012-08-03.flac16_mk22** (recommended): source not stated; 29 songs; 163 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The audio quality is described as top notch for the Red Rocks venue [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Trombone Shorty and Band of Horses performed opening acts for the main set [1]\n- Strong winds blew through the PA system during the final songs of the concert [1]\n- The performance was part of a solid two-night run by the band [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2012-08-03.flac16_mk22**: taped by Coloartist; transferred by Bennett Schwartz; source: Schoeps MK22>Kwon NOS>KC5>CMC6>analog>788T (HPF 0) 24/48 [1]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps MK22 microphones into Kwon NOS preamp, then CMC6 and 788T [1]",
